 | `Rule30BlackPhaseEscape` | 2026-11-09 | Universal black-phase escape. At a black center time the next center value is the negation of the left neighbour, whatever the right half: `center (t + 1) = ! cell t (-1)`. `UBE` (**open**): every finite nonzero left start, driven by every periodic word `w` with a black phase (`Rule30DrivenLeft.L w s`), eventually fails that forced value, `L w s t (-1) ≠ ! w (t + 1)` at some black phase `t`. `UBE` gives `Problem1` (`problem1_of_UBE`) through the same statement on the actual cone rows, `BlackEscapeOnCone` (`blackEscape_of_UBE`, `problem1_of_blackEscape`). The all-black word escapes by time `m + 1` (`allBlack_escape`, from `Rule30DrivenLeft.ones_fails`). Against the kit's other reductions: `UBE` implies `Rule30Coupled.CQ ω` for every periodic `ω` with a black phase, the hypothesis of `Rule30Coupled.problem1_of_CQ` (`CQ_of_UBE`), and implies `Rule30PeriodTwo.Q01`, which is its instance for the word black at even times, since under that word an admissible driven left half is the zero-driven one (`Q01_of_UBE`). Neither converse is known: `CQ ω` also asks for a finite right half coupled to `ω`, and `Q01` is one word. Nothing here proves `UBE`. Contributed by AIOvernight with Claude (Anthropic) and OpenAI Codex as Rule 30 Prize submission [R30-20261104-fec9b8](https://www.wolframcloud.com/obj/rule-30-prize/Agents/status/R30-20261104-fec9b8). `CQ_of_UBE` and `Q01_of_UBE` were added for the kit. | `problem1_of_UBE`, `problem1_of_blackEscape`, `blackEscape_of_UBE`, `allBlack_escape`, `CQ_of_UBE`, `Q01_of_UBE` |
 | `Rule30PeriodTwoMass` | 2026-11-09 | A mass conjecture for period 2. If the center column were eventually `1, 0, 1, 0, …`, the left half-row at a late white time of column `-1` would be a natural number `X` (bit `i` = cell `-1-i`) under the zero-wall map `Rule30ZeroBoundary.IntegerForm.F`, and its wall trace would be a G word at every length: white at time `0`, black at the odd times, no two consecutive white even times (`lang_G`, from `Rule30PeriodTwo.m1_even` and `golden`). So period 2 is excluded if no natural seed has an infinite G trace (`not_eventually_period_two_of_noSeed`). This hypothesis is about the left half alone; it follows from `Rule30SeparatorQ01.QN` (a short argument, not included in this module), which is equivalent to `SEP` (`Rule30SeparatorQ01.sep_iff_QN`, `Rule30SeparatorEquivalences.separator_equivalence`). It also follows from any linear bound `Z ≤ c·A + d` on the finite G words, with `Z` the number of white even times and `A` the seed weight (`MassBound`, `not_eventually_period_two_of_massbound`), from any positive linear floor `H ≤ q·A + d` (`MassFloor`, `not_eventually_period_two_of_floor`), and from Conjecture S: every G word of length `H ≥ 2` has `7·A ≥ H + 4` (`ConjS`, `not_eventually_period_two_of_S`; the even form `7·A ≥ H + 5` at even `H` implies it, `ConjS_of_even`). Conjecture S and the floor and mass-bound hypotheses are **open**. The kernel checks S for every `H ≤ 90`, in its even form at even `H` (`S_upto_90`): an exhaustive search over the seeds, evaluated in `Rule30Certificates.PeriodTwoMass` and proved to imply a plain search whose soundness is `dfs_sound`. The constant `7` is sharp: seeds at `H = 86, 198, 310` have `7·A = H + 5` and stay G words at `H + 1` with `7·A = H + 4` (`sharp_86`, `sharp_198`, `sharp_310`); they are truncations of the 2-adic seed `2538/127` with the last block changed. The tail law: the preimage transducer of `F` has 4 states, the composites along nonempty words lie in an explicit list of 40 maps (`comp_mem`), all of whose cycles have length 1, 2 or 3 (`cyc_div6`, `no_four_cycle`), and two preimage runs of one word that never share a state carry at least `2n` ones on every `3n` consecutive positions (`mass_two_thirds`). Contributed by AIOvernight with Claude (Anthropic) and OpenAI Codex as Rule 30 Prize submission [R30-20261109-4dce4d](https://www.wolframcloud.com/obj/rule-30-prize/Agents/status/R30-20261109-4dce4d). | `not_eventually_period_two_of_S`, `not_eventually_period_two_of_floor`, `not_eventually_period_two_of_massbound`, `not_eventually_period_two_of_noSeed`, `ConjS_of_even`, `S_upto_90`, `sharp_86`, `sharp_198`, `sharp_310`, `comp_mem`, `cyc_div6`, `no_four_cycle`, `mass_two_thirds` |
 | `Rule30PeriodTwoNoFloor` | 2026-11-09 | No density floor for the left half that is the same for every periodic center pattern. For a center pattern `c`, a finite seed `X` (bit `i` = depth `i + 1`) is `GValid c X H` when its driven evolution keeps the kick rules K1–K3 for `H` steps; `Eternal c x` is the same for ever for an infinite row. `c9`, of period `72`, is the center word beside a single black cell on a ring of `9` cells (`c9_ring`); `c14`, of period `1428`, the same on a ring of `14` (`c14_ring`). The row black exactly at depths `8, 17, 26, …` is eternal beside `c9` (`eternal_row_c9`), the row black at depths `14, 28, …` beside `c14` (`eternal_row_c14`), with weights `(H + 1) / 9` and `H / 14` below depth `H` (`weight_row9`, `weight_row14`). So every truncation is a finite `GValid` word of every length with that weight (`trunc_valid_c9`, `trunc_valid_c14`), and no floor `H ≤ q · A + d` with `q < 9` (resp. `q < 14`) holds on the finite `GValid` words of these patterns (`no_floor_c9`, `no_floor_c14`, `no_uniform_floor`): a floor common to all periodic patterns is at most `1/14`. The rows are infinite, so they do not contradict `Rule30Coupled.CQ`; the result is a barrier for one kind of argument, a density floor with one constant for every pattern, next to `Rule30ZeroBoundaryBarriers` and the control `Rule30AlternatingTraceBridge.alternatingCenter_without_finiteSupport`. Per-pattern floors are untouched, and the finite form is open; measured, not proved: cut to `n` bits, these rows survive only about `n + O(1)` steps beyond their length. Method: read sideways, rule 30 determines column `d + 2` from columns `d + 1` and `d`; if the center column and the wall trace are `Q`-periodic and the column pair at depth `n` equals that at depth `0`, the space-time is periodic in time and depth (`orbF_sideways`, `crystal`), so validity reduces to one period, checked by kernel evaluation; eternal rows are `GValid` at every length (`gvalid_of_eternal`). Contributed by AIOvernight with Claude (Anthropic) and OpenAI Codex as Rule 30 Prize submission [R30-20261109-ec5566](https://www.wolframcloud.com/obj/rule-30-prize/Agents/status/R30-20261109-ec5566). | `eternal_row_c9`, `eternal_row_c14`, `weight_row9`, `weight_row14`, `trunc_valid_c9`, `trunc_valid_c14`, `no_floor_c9`, `no_floor_c14`, `no_uniform_floor`, `c9_ring`, `c14_ring`, `orbF_sideways`, `crystal`, `gvalid_of_eternal` |
+| `Rule30ConeTip` | 2026-11-10 | The cone tip of the zero-boundary left half. For every `t ≥ 2` and every row `L`, the second difference of the depth-1 cell `zrow L t 1` in the depths `t - 1` and `t` (`flip`) is `t - 1` modulo `2`, the same on every row (`cone_tip`). A cell reads its deepest input with coefficient `1` (`level_aff`), so flipping depth `d` changes the cells of level `d + 1` by the negated cells of level `d - 1` (`diag`, `chain`), and those flip with depth `d - 1` while the wall stays white (`chain_flip`). For even `t`, every function with vanishing second differences in those directions, every affine function in particular (`affine_second`), misses the tip somewhere on each face of four rows (`face_disagree`), so the tip is not affine (`tip_not_affine`). The mechanism is the left-permutive derivative of `Rule30Equivalents.AlgebraicDegree`, here in the row frame with its white wall. Contributed by Gareth Herbert with Claude (Anthropic) and GPT (OpenAI), as Rule 30 Prize submission [R30-20261110-b07808](https://www.wolframcloud.com/obj/rule-30-prize/Agents/status/R30-20261110-b07808). | `level_aff`, `diag`, `chain_flip`, `cone_tip`, `face_disagree`, `affine_second`, `tip_not_affine` |
 | `Rule30PeriodTwoLadder` | 2026-11-09 | The left half-row as a natural number `X` driven by a prescribed center `c`, with the kick rules K1–K3 on prefixes (`GValid`); the official left half-row is valid for ever beside the official center (`gvalid_rowNat`). For the period-2 pattern `p01`: the model's zero-driven half is `Rule30DrivenLeft.L (fun _ => false)` (`orb_zero_eq_L`, `orb_p01_eq_orb_zero`), `Rule30PeriodTwo.Q01` implies `NoSeed p01` (`noSeed01_of_Q01`), and `NoSeed p01` excludes an eventual period 2 (`not_eventually_period_two_of_noSeed01`). Adding `2^t` to a seed flips exactly one antidiagonal of its evolution (`orb_flip`, `kick_flip`, `gvalid_flip`), so the seeds `Z`, `2^H + Z` together contribute the transition count of a fair-coin chain (`pair_count`). The Mean Ladder Law: over all `2^l` fillings of the next `l` seed digits, the number valid to `n + l` is exactly a coin-chain count (`mean_ladder`, `fill_eq`), and exactly `fib ((H + 1) / 2 + 2)` seeds below `2^H` are valid to `H` (`card_valid`). `Rule30ZeroBoundary.count_constrained` counts `2 ^ ⌊W / 2⌋` zero-boundary starts that keep column `-1` black at the even steps; `card_valid` instead counts the seeds that obey the kick rules beside `p01`, and gets a Fibonacci number. The coin ladder is the sum of the survivor counts over all digit blocks, and the true ladder `S n l` is the zero block alone (`ladder_average`, `S_le_Scoin`). `NoSeed p01` holds iff `S n l` reaches `0` for every bitlength `n` (`noSeed_iff_S_eventually_zero`). So a ladder bound `S n (2 j) · 2^j ≤ C · V n` in natural numbers, or `S n (2 j) ≤ C · V n · θ^j` with rational `0 ≤ θ < 1`, would exclude period 2 (`noSeed_of_half_ladder_bound`, `noSeed_of_geometric_ladder_bound`, `not_eventually_period_two_of_ladder_bound`, `not_eventually_period_two_of_geometric_ladder_bound`). These bounds and `NoSeed p01` are **open**: the law is exact only on average over digit blocks, and a finite seed is the all-zero block. Contributed by AIOvernight with Claude (Anthropic) and OpenAI Codex as Rule 30 Prize submission [R30-20261109-2c50a4](https://www.wolframcloud.com/obj/rule-30-prize/Agents/status/R30-20261109-2c50a4). | `mean_ladder`, `fill_eq`, `ladder_average`, `S_le_Scoin`, `pair_count`, `card_valid`, `orb_flip`, `kick_flip`, `gvalid_flip`, `orb_zero_eq_L`, `orb_p01_eq_orb_zero`, `noSeed01_of_Q01`, `not_eventually_period_two_of_noSeed01`, `gvalid_rowNat`, `noSeed_iff_S_eventually_zero`, `noSeed_of_half_ladder_bound`, `noSeed_of_geometric_ladder_bound`, `not_eventually_period_two_of_ladder_bound`, `not_eventually_period_two_of_geometric_ladder_bound` |
 | `Rule30PeriodTwoWidth13` | 2026-11-09 | Period 2: every right half forces the left trace into a nine-pair gap language. Under an alternating center, read from every late white time of column `-1`, the left trace lies in `GE2` at every length (`lang_GE2`): column `-1` is black at the black center times, the white cells of column `-1` at the white center times are `2`, `3`, `4` or `5` pairs of steps apart, and consecutive gaps form one of the nine pairs `22 24 25 33 35 45 52 53 55`. The columns `1..13` and the center form a strip of `16384` nodes with column `14` free, so the statement holds for every right half, finite or not; the kernel checks a rank certificate of its condensation and, in its two recurrent levels, an inductive set of states of a gap automaton (`certOK_true`, data in `Rule30Certificates/PeriodTwoWidth13`). One level is the E2 language; the other (gap `4` only) would make column `-1` eventually 8-periodic, which a finite left half excludes (`tr_not_eventually_periodic`); the kicks are never eventually periodic (`kicks_not_eventually_periodic`). This is sharper than the width-5 and width-6 languages of `Rule30PeriodTwoLanguage` and `Rule30PeriodTwoWidth6.col1_constraints`, and is the period-2 counterpart of `Rule30PeriodThreeLanguage`. `NoSeedGE2`, that no finite left seed keeps all its trace prefixes in `GE2`, is a left-only statement that excludes period 2 (`not_eventually_period_two_of_noSeed_GE2`) and follows from `Rule30PeriodTwo.Q01` (`noSeed_GE2_of_Q01`, through `L_zero_eq_iterate`; `not_eventually_period_two_of_Q01_via_E2`): a weaker open hypothesis with no assumption on the right half. A bound on the even-time zeros of the finite `GE2` words by a function of the seed weight gives `NoSeedGE2` (`noSeed_GE2_of_massBoundFun`, `not_eventually_period_two_of_E2_fun`, linear form `not_eventually_period_two_of_E2`). For the coupled question, an open right dichotomy `RD` (every finite right half enters `Rule30GateTrap.trap` at a white time or has eventually periodic column `1` at the white times) with `Rule30GateTrap.Q01Gap` gives `Rule30PeriodTwoCoupled.CQ01` (`CQ01_of_RD_of_Q01Gap`, `no_eventual_period_two_of_RD_of_Q01Gap`). `NoSeedGE2`, `RD`, `Q01Gap` and `Q01` are **open**. Contributed by AIOvernight with Claude (Anthropic) and OpenAI Codex as Rule 30 Prize submission [R30-20261109-62afca](https://www.wolframcloud.com/obj/rule-30-prize/Agents/status/R30-20261109-62afca). | `lang_GE2`, `certOK_true`, `not_eventually_period_two_of_noSeed_GE2`, `noSeed_GE2_of_Q01`, `not_eventually_period_two_of_Q01_via_E2`, `L_zero_eq_iterate`, `not_eventually_period_two_of_E2_fun`, `not_eventually_period_two_of_E2`, `noSeed_GE2_of_massBoundFun`, `kicks_not_eventually_periodic`, `tr_not_eventually_periodic`, `CQ01_of_RD_of_Q01Gap`, `no_eventual_period_two_of_RD_of_Q01Gap` |
 
